WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:04.237
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER): With
one day until chef James and I

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.040
battle for the honor of
being deemed Yoopers,

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:09.743
I'm off to meet a man
who's famous for three

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:13.646
words you don't normally hear
together: Smoked fish sausages.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:16.716
Now sounds a bit mad doesn't
it, smoked fish sausage?

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:20.653
But if you're a Yooper,
it's a tradition.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.355
Hopefully, it's a
secret that I can

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:26.226
take with me to the final cook.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:29.896
Where in the hell does
this baby plug into?

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.964
Captain Ron.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.766
Well, how are you doing, bud.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:33.833
I've been waiting for you.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.335
Oh, my goodness me.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.504
Yeah, you want to come
see what the Yoopers do?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.839
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
Captain Ron has made fish

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.274
sausages since he was a boy.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.144
This week is about
becoming a Yooper?

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.479
And they said you've
got the best smoked fish

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.248
sausage anywhere in the UP.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.816
Yep, I'll put it
up against anybody.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.585
Now, I could smell that smoke
sausage from down the road.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.888
Oh yeah, We get a lot of
people selling that up there.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:57.524
So this could be a key
ingredient for my final cook.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.258
Yep.

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.626
Yeah, here we go, bud.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.360
Let's go.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:01.694
They're little babies.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.430
Oh, my Lord.

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.164
Stop it.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.064
That's a trout?

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.199
That's a lake trout.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.801
Captain Ron, that's huge.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.768
Oh Yeah.

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:09.903
You sure that's trout?

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.038
That's lake trout right there.

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.072
That's incredible.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.841
Have you ever filleted a fish?

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.477
100,000 times, absolutely.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.879
OK, there's your
good knife right there.

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:21.014
I got you a good sharp on.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:21.915
Watch out.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.983
Yes, very carefully.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.019
You gotta take the
rib bones off there.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.020
Yep, right there see?

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:27.654
[bleep]

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:28.855
Man.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.290
Yeah, I don't want that
going through the grinder

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.524
because we don't want to eat it.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.292
No.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.126
You gotta big bone there.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.294
See it?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.261
Man, you're missing
nothing are you?

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.563
There's no flies on you--

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.430
Oh no, I've been doing
it all my life, bud.

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.398
Gotcha

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.165
My one eye can
see better than you.

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.366
[laughing]

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.502
That one eye is a
powerful eye, man.

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.770
I'm telling you very powerful.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.672
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
Fish filleted.

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:46.773
Not bad for a troll.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.875
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
It's time to start

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.910
seeing how the sausage is made.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.111
OK.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.680
Now, we just gotta grind her.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.948
[grinder whirring]

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.382
And then we got that.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.787
All right.

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:03.923
Come on, get in there
you little prick.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.025
I swear a little
bit at it all time.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.627
You hear what he said?

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.395
GORDON RAMSEY
(VOICEOVER): Turns out

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.065
I'm not the only potty mouth
chef in this neck of the woods.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.399
I'm a clean nut, too.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.468
GORDON RAMSEY: We can't
work on a dirty surface.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.303
[bleep] no.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.739
All right, now we can mix.

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:22.475
I got secret ingredients
I can't even tell you.

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:24.844
I can tell you, but
I'd have to drown you.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.547
If I'm going to become a
Yooper, I need to know the se--

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.048
Give me a few
secret ingredients.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.884
I got some salt in there.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.118
Salt. That's not a secret.

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.120
Smell that right now.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.388
Old Spice?

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:36.756
Oh no.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.424
That's [bleep] stuff.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.392
[laughing]

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.126
Ginger?

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.694
Nope.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:42.795
Curry powder?

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:43.863
Nope.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.797
Nutmeg?

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.100
Yep, there you go.

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:48.401
So you gotta give a little oil.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:49.569
And mix it up with a hand?

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.770
Well, no.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.372
I'll get something-- You
want [inaudible],, right?

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:53.339
[interposing voices]

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.774
I'll mix it with my hand.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.309
You might have been pickin'
your ass, I don't know.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.677
We can't mix like that.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:02:58.945
My hands are clean.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.380
Captain Ron, look
at those hands.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:01.447
OK.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:02.181
Let 'em have it.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.716
Absolutely.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.318
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
Nutmeg and secret spices added.

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:07.353
It's time to start
the casing process.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.521
GORDON RAMSEY: Gotcha.

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:09.856
CAPTAIN RON: That's
probably good.

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.124
This is where
the magic starts.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.659
Yeah, crank that baby.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.459
Ready.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.761
Oh, you're going backwards.

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.062
OK.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.797
Holy [bleep] now you
just went backwards.

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:18.731
What the hell.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:19.465
It's coming out.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:19.999
It's coming.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:20.767
It's coming.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:21.534
It's coming.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.035
It's coming.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:22.936
That see?

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:23.703
Yes, see [inaudible].

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:24.971
That's nice.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:25.805
See that's far enough,
and you tie that.

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:26.673
Yep, there you go.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.508
Then tie that nice.

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.944
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
Casing complete, it's time

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.512
to put them into
the wood smoker,

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.747
which is filled
with more of Captain

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:36.883
Ron's secret ingredients.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.251
Now what flavor is this?

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:40.186
That's just Captain
Ron's flavor.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.388
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
I'm too afraid to ask what

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:44.624
Captain Ron's flavoring is.

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.526
So how long will
they smoke in there.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.728
That one's maybe
like six hours,

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.997
but I got something for
you in there right now.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:51.965
You got some ready?

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:53.099
I got some ready for ya.

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.033
Inside here?

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.501
Inside their.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.904
[coughing]

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.238
I know what that's about, bud.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.807
Yeah, you always get smoke.

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.775
If you want to be a Yooper,
you got to get in there, buddy.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.911
GORDON RAMSEY (VOICEOVER):
Having been immersed

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.346
in Captain Ron's
flavor, whatever

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:09.983
that is, it's time to taste
the fruits of our labor.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.050
I love--

00:04:11.117 --> 00:04:12.352
Look at how nice that is.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.653
--how juicy they are.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.689
Oh Yeah, That'll
put hair on your nuts.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.524
[laughing]

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.525
It will.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:24.998
That's some good [bleep].

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.466
That's lovely.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:27.934
See, and it won't break
apart when you cut it either.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.168
Cook, may I take those three?

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.203
Yes, you can.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:31.838
That was incredible.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:32.939
They said, it was the best.

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:34.374
Having tasted it now--

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.608
Yeah.

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:36.776
--for me I think it's
going to be a little secret

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:37.543
weapon for the final cook.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:38.111
There you go.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:38.978
Sir, take care.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:40.680
Take care, bud.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:41.781
What a sausage.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.449
The spice is perfect.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:47.153
But after that smoke, the
flavor and the moisture inside--

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.722
so it's giving me ideas now.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:54.594
I don't think James will
have that at his final cook.

